'=====================================================================
' Agent name : BulkReg\09 - Reconcile
' Version    : 4.4.0  (BulkReg release; libraries BulkRegCommon + BulkRegAgents 4.4.0)
' Code       : ALL logic is in the script library BulkRegAgents (BR_RunReconcile).
'              This agent only calls it, so it never changes between releases.
'
' HOW TO INSTALL: open the agent, click in the editor, Ctrl+A, Delete, paste this
'              WHOLE file, Ctrl+S. Designer puts each part in its place automatically.
' Designer   : Shared agent, LotusScript
'              Runtime: On event > Action menu selection, Target: None
'              (NOT 'All selected documents' - Designer's default - or Notes asks for a selected document)
'              (backslash in the name = Actions > BulkReg submenu; do NOT use '|')
'
' What it does (details: BulkRegAgents > BR_RunReconcile):
'
' READ-ONLY reconciliation, written to CSV files (ReconcileDir, default <BaseDir>\reconcile\):
'   RECON_<run>_all.csv           one row per directory user, with Status and recommended Action
'   RECON_<run>_missing_users.csv users not registered (and why) / users of your expected list not in the directory
'   RECON_<run>_missing_mail.csv  registered users whose mailbox is missing, incomplete or not recorded
'   RECON_<run>_orphan_mail.csv   mail files in the numbered mail folders that no Person document uses
'   RECON_<run>_summary.txt       counts per status
' 4.3.0: also RECON_<run>_gaps.csv (not registered / no mail / no vault / duplicate; scope file for 08) and _duplicates.csv.
' Optional input: a CSV of the users that SHOULD exist (column ShortName / InternetAddress / FullName).
' Also flags Person items (JobTitle, FirstName, ...) with extra blanks. Changes nothing in Domino.
'=====================================================================
'#####################################################################
' --- part 1: (Options) ---
'#####################################################################
Option Public
Option Declare
Use "BulkRegAgents"
'#####################################################################
' --- part 2: Initialize ---
'#####################################################################
Sub Initialize
	Call BR_RunReconcile()
End Sub
